# Booleans without a boolean type: langlib original.
#
# K is true and SK is false, because a conditional is just the choice of
# an argument: K t e reduces to t, and SK t e reduces to e. The term
# below is the false branch of that choice applied to S and I, so it
# reduces to I. Swap the leading SK for a K and it reduces to S instead.
SK S I
